1. Datasets shipped inside the APK (app/src/main/assets/, app/src/main/res/raw/)
================================================================================

devices.json — device model catalog
  Source:    https://github.com/KHwang9883/MobileModels-csv
  License:   Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0
             International (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
             https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/
  Revision:  recorded verbatim, together with the attribution text, in
             app/src/main/assets/devices.NOTICE.txt (do not edit either file;
             app/src/test/.../BaselineDataParityTest.kt pins both byte-for-byte
             against the digest lock in app/src/test/resources/baseline/)

  ** Consequence for anyone redistributing this repository **
  The NC element means the *bundled dataset* may not be used for commercial
  purposes, and the SA element means derivative databases must be shared under
  the same license. While this file ships inside app/src/main/assets/, the
  combined work (app + assets) inherits that restriction, regardless of the
  Apache-2.0 grant on the code. Treat code and data as separately licensed, and
  drop or replace this asset before any commercial distribution. This repository
  has no clean-room generator for the catalog, so "replace it" is real work
  tracked as an open item, not a switch to flip.

carriers.json — MCC/MNC carrier catalog
  Source:    https://github.com/pbakondy/mcc-mnc-list
  License:   MIT (full text and upstream revision recorded in
             app/src/main/assets/carriers.NOTICE.txt)
  Notes:     The upstream dataset derives its numbering from ITU-T E.121
             (https://www.itu.int/rec/T-REC-E.212/en). Rows are used read-only
             to fill SIM operator fields of a spoof profile.

================================================================================
2. Reference baseline used by the parity gate (NOT redistributed)
================================================================================

third_party/Guise_Reborn-main
  A local copy of the Guise Reborn project is used only as a byte-parity
  baseline for the shipped catalogs above. It is gitignored and is NOT part of
  this repository's distribution. Contributors who want to run the deeper
  cross-check (app/src/test/.../BaselineDataParityTest.kt →
  lock_matchesBaselineOnDisk_whenBaselineIsPresent) fetch it locally; its own
  upstream license then governs that copy. The parity assertion itself runs on a
  fresh clone without it, against the checked-in digest lock.

